<title>USA: U.S. credit rating agencies open on Good Friday.</title>
<headline>U.S. credit rating agencies open on Good Friday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. credit rating agencies Standard and Poor's and Moody's Investors Service Inc both said they will be open on Good Friday, March 28.</p>
<p>S&amp;P will conduct a normal business day in the U.S., operating from 0800 EST/1300 GMT to 1800 EST/2300 GMT, while Moody's said it will have a shortened day from 0900 EST/1400 GMT to 1300 EST/1800 GMT.</p>
<p>The U.S. Treasury and related debt markets will be closed for the Good Friday holiday.</p>
<p>(( -- C. Trokie, U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678))</p>
